  "description": "COSKON crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21. Reported CIF formula moiety: C166 H116 Er4 O40 P9 1+,7.5(C2 H6 O1),5.5(H2 O1),0.5(Cl1 1-),0.5(H1 O1 1-). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er5 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er6 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er7 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er8 (Er) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 8 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 4.290-4.363 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 124.24-127.46°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Er4(PO4)(R-L)8(EtOH)3(H2O)]Cl(OH)·15EtOH·11H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
